{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[{"file_id":"1NwqfqQWknDy-qEQvK0HhH5lGZvcYsmW0","timestamp":1697744373588}],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyPLE/36Pft3O1pj8Qywh2Ic"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","# Redes Neuronales SOM | Clasificación de Billetes con Python\n","\n","### Implementación de mapas autoorganizados para el análisis y clasificación de datos\n","\n","**Área:** Inteligencia Artificial | Machine Learning | Redes Neuronales  \n","**Lenguaje:** Python  \n","**Entorno:** Google Colab  \n","**Técnica:** Self-Organizing Maps (SOM)\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Descripción del proyecto\n","\n","Este notebook desarrolla una implementación práctica de una **red neuronal de mapas autoorganizados (Self-Organizing Map, SOM)** para analizar y clasificar billetes mediante características estadísticas extraídas de imágenes.\n","\n","Se utiliza el conjunto de datos **Banknote Authentication**, disponible en el repositorio de aprendizaje automático de la Universidad de California, Irvine (UCI).\n","\n","El objetivo es comprender el funcionamiento de las redes neuronales no supervisadas y explorar cómo pueden organizar información multidimensional en un mapa bidimensional, permitiendo identificar patrones y realizar una clasificación posterior mediante etiquetas.\n","\n","## Objetivos\n","\n","- Comprender el funcionamiento de los mapas autoorganizados (SOM).\n","- Preparar y normalizar los datos utilizando MinMaxScaler.\n","- Dividir el conjunto de datos en entrenamiento (80%) y prueba (20%).\n","- Implementar las distancias euclidiana y Manhattan.\n","- Identificar la neurona ganadora mediante Best Matching Unit (BMU).\n","- Configurar una red neuronal SOM de 10 × 10 neuronas.\n","- Entrenar el mapa mediante 50,000 iteraciones.\n","- Asignar etiquetas a las neuronas utilizando las clases predominantes.\n","- Visualizar la distribución de clases en un mapa de colores.\n","- Evaluar las predicciones mediante la métrica de exactitud (Accuracy).\n","\n","## Metodología\n","\n","**1. Preparación de datos**\n","\n","Se carga el conjunto de datos Banknote Authentication y se separan cuatro características numéricas de sus respectivas etiquetas de clasificación.\n","\n","**2. Normalización**\n","\n","Se utiliza MinMaxScaler para transformar los valores de entrada a un intervalo de 0 a 1.\n","\n","**3. Construcción del modelo SOM**\n","\n","Se inicializa un mapa de 100 neuronas distribuidas en una cuadrícula de 10 × 10, con pesos aleatorios y cuatro dimensiones por neurona.\n","\n","**4. Entrenamiento**\n","\n","Durante 50,000 iteraciones se seleccionan muestras aleatorias, se identifica la neurona ganadora mediante distancia euclidiana y se actualizan los pesos de las neuronas de su vecindario.\n","\n","La tasa de aprendizaje y el rango de vecindad disminuyen progresivamente durante el entrenamiento.\n","\n","**5. Etiquetado y visualización**\n","\n","Después del entrenamiento, se asignan etiquetas a las neuronas según la clase más frecuente de las muestras asociadas. Las neuronas sin observaciones reciben una etiqueta especial.\n","\n","Posteriormente, se genera una representación gráfica del mapa utilizando diferentes colores.\n","\n","**6. Evaluación del modelo**\n","\n","Se utiliza el conjunto de prueba para identificar las neuronas ganadoras, generar predicciones y calcular la exactitud de clasificación mediante Accuracy Score.\n","\n","## Tecnologías utilizadas\n","\n","**Python | NumPy | SciPy | Scikit-learn | Matplotlib | Google Colab**\n","\n","## Aplicaciones\n","\n","Los mapas autoorganizados permiten explorar relaciones entre observaciones multidimensionales y pueden utilizarse en:\n","\n","- Análisis exploratorio y agrupamiento de datos.\n","- Visualización de patrones multidimensionales.\n","- Segmentación de información.\n","- Identificación de similitudes entre observaciones.\n","- Construcción de sistemas experimentales de clasificación.\n","\n","## Conclusión\n","\n","Este ejercicio permite comprender cómo una red neuronal SOM puede organizar datos multidimensionales en una estructura bidimensional mediante aprendizaje no supervisado.\n","\n","Además, demuestra cómo incorporar etiquetas posteriormente para realizar tareas de clasificación y evaluar el comportamiento del modelo con datos de prueba.\n","\n","El procedimiento representa una aplicación práctica de redes neuronales, procesamiento numérico y visualización de datos utilizando Python.\n","\n","---\n","\n","**Autor:** Data Engineer Luis Barahona  \n","**Institución:** Universidad del Caribe, México  \n","**GitHub:** [LuisBarahonaMX](https://github.com/LuisBarahonaMX)\n","\n","**Dataset:** [Banknote Authentication — UCI Machine Learning Repository](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/267/banknote+authentication)\n","\n","**Categoría:** Machine Learning | Neural Networks | Self-Organizing Maps\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ls1-7fbGcKOE"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"4_O3isowbWfm"},"outputs":[],"source":["\n","# importar librerías\n","import numpy as np\n","from numpy.ma.core import ceil\n","from scipy.spatial import distance\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n","from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from matplotlib import animation, colors\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# montar Google drive\n","from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/content/drive/')\n"],"metadata":{"id":"onKrzrlRbcaq"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# datos utilizado en este ejemplo\n","# banknote authentication Data Set\n","# https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/banknote+authentication\n","# Dua, D. and Graff, C. (2019). UCI Machine Learning Repository [http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml].\n","# Irvine, CA: University of California, School of Information and Computer Science.\n","\n","data_file = \"data_banknote_authentication.txt\"\n","path_file = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Datasets/\""],"metadata":{"id":"eGAHfWuobmpZ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# datos\n","data_x = np.loadtxt(path_file+data_file,\n","    delimiter=\",\", skiprows=0, usecols=range(0,4),\n","    dtype=np.float64)\n","\n","print(data_x)"],"metadata":{"id":"b8Xqlsu_bqQh"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["[[  3.6216    8.6661   -2.8073   -0.44699]\n"," [  4.5459    8.1674   -2.4586   -1.4621 ]\n"," [  3.866    -2.6383    1.9242    0.10645]\n"," ...\n"," [ -3.7503  -13.4586   17.5932   -2.7771 ]\n"," [ -3.5637   -8.3827   12.393    -1.2823 ]\n"," [ -2.5419   -0.65804   2.6842    1.1952 ]]"],"metadata":{"id":"0ahLgZp2bstx"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# clases\n","data_y = np.loadtxt(path_file+data_file,\n","          delimiter=\",\", skiprows=0, usecols=(4,),\n","                    dtype=np.int64)\n","print(data_y)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"emsCXikTbu3p"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# datos de entrenamiento y prueba\n","train_x, test_x, train_y, test_y = \\\n","      train_test_split(data_x, data_y, test_size=0.2,\n","      random_state=42)\n","\n","print(train_x.shape, train_y.shape,\n","      test_x.shape, test_y.shape)"],"metadata":{"id":"wbKcs4EIbvyh"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# normalización de datos\n","def normalizacion(data):\n","  escalar = MinMaxScaler()\n","  escalado = escalar.fit_transform(data)\n","  return escalado"],"metadata":{"id":"WEQDKj24bzmR"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# distancia Euclideana\n","def dist_Euclideana(x,y):\n","  return distance.euclidean(x,y)"],"metadata":{"id":"ii51dgo2b12R"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# distancia de Manhattan\n","def dist_Manhattan(x,y):\n","  return distance.cityblock(x,y)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"QJkl_Dhnb4Ry"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# busca la neurona ganadora dentro del mapa (som)\n","# Best Matching Unit search (BMUS)\n","# t = indice de muestra aleatoria de entrenamiento\n","def BMUS(data, t, som):\n","  ganadora = [0,0]\n","  # inicializa con la distancia más grande\n","  dist_mascorta = np.sqrt(data.shape[1])\n","  # distancia más corta de la muestra con los valores en el mapa\n","  for row in range(som.shape[0]):\n","    for col in range(som.shape[1]):\n","      # calcula la distancia Euclideana\n","      distancia = dist_Euclideana(som[row][col], data[t])\n","      # checa si encontro una distancia más corta\n","      if distancia < dist_mascorta:\n","        # actualiza la distancia más corta\n","        dist_mascorta = distancia\n","        # coordenadas de la celda\n","        ganadora = [row,col]\n","  # regresa las coordenadas de la celda\n","  return ganadora"],"metadata":{"id":"kxhwCjeMb67x"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# tasa de aprendizaje y rango de vecindad\n","def decaimiento(iter, max_iters, max_tasa_aprendizaje,\n","                max_m_distancia):\n","  coeficiente = 1.0 - (np.float64(iter) / max_iters)\n","  tasa_aprendizaje = coeficiente * max_tasa_aprendizaje\n","  rango_vecindario = ceil(coeficiente * max_m_distancia)\n","  return tasa_aprendizaje, rango_vecindario"],"metadata":{"id":"srTBDHVjb9-K"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# normalización de datos de entrenamiento\n","train_x_norm = normalizacion(train_x)\n","print(\"mínimo: \", np.min(train_x_norm))\n","print(\"máximo: \", np.max(train_x_norm))"],"metadata":{"id":"lDbJq9aOcAG4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# initialización SOM\n","\n","# número de dimensiones en los datos de entrada\n","num_dims = train_x_norm.shape[1]\n","print(num_dims)\n","np.random.seed(7)"],"metadata":{"id":"BeYSCgvNcCCg"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# hiperparametros\n","num_filas = 10\n","num_cols = 10\n","max_m_distancia = 4\n","max_tasa_aprendizaje = 0.5\n","max_iters = int(5*10e3) #50000"],"metadata":{"id":"zvxDPz8dcEXY"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# construcción de SOM\n","# pesos aleatorios en el rango de [0,1]\n","som = np.random.random_sample(size=(num_filas, num_cols,\n","                                    num_dims))\n","print(\"SOM con dimensiones de: \",som.shape)\n","print(f\"El valor mínimo es de {np.min(som)}, \\\n","        y \\nel valor máximo es de {np.max(som)}\")\n"],"metadata":{"id":"XjVh0BCecG6p"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["print(som)\n"],"metadata":{"id":"9-FBLG3zcLR5"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# entrenamiento de SOM\n","for iteracion in range(max_iters):\n","  # cada 1000 iteraciones\n","  if (iteracion+1) % 1000 == 0:\n","    # imprime la iteración actual\n","    print(\"Iteración: \", iteracion+1)\n","  # tasa de aprendizaje y vecindario decaen con el tiempo\n","  tasa_aprendizaje, rango_vecindario = decaimiento(iteracion,\n","        max_iters, max_tasa_aprendizaje, max_m_distancia)\n","  # muestra aleatoria de entrenamiento en cada iteración\n","  t = np.random.randint(0,high=train_x_norm.shape[0])\n","  # busca neurona ganadora (coordenadas de la celda)\n","  neurona_ganadora = BMUS(train_x_norm, t, som)\n","  # recorre el mapa (som)\n","  for fila in range(som.shape[0]):\n","    for col in range(som.shape[1]):\n","      # distancia Manhattan o de Block\n","      if dist_Manhattan([fila,col],neurona_ganadora) <= \\\n","        rango_vecindario:\n","        # actualiza el peso del vecindario\n","        som[fila][col] += \\\n","            tasa_aprendizaje*(train_x_norm[t] - som[fila][col])\n","print(\"Entrenamiento de SOM completado.\")"],"metadata":{"id":"-ykjyj-QcPJH"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# mapa\n","mapa = np.empty(shape=(num_filas, num_cols), dtype=object)\n","mapa.shape\n"],"metadata":{"id":"2vocgH8FcRn3"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","\n","# lista vacia para guardar las etiquetas\n","for fila in range(num_filas):\n","  for col in range(num_cols):\n","    mapa[fila][col] = []\n","\n","print(mapa)"],"metadata":{"id":"7jXHEmRLcXiG"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# etiqueta de la neurona ganadora\n","for d in range(train_x_norm.shape[0]):\n","  ganadora = BMUS(train_x_norm, d, som)\n","  mapa[ganadora[0]][ganadora[1]].append(train_y[d])\n","\n","print(mapa)"],"metadata":{"id":"F6rxYZjVcbJN"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# construcción de mapa de etiquetas\n","mapa_etiquetas = np.zeros(shape=(num_filas, num_cols),\n","                          dtype=np.int64)\n","for fila in range(num_filas):\n","  for col in range(num_cols):\n","    lista_etiquetas = mapa[fila][col]\n","    if len(lista_etiquetas)==0:\n","      etiqueta = 2\n","    else:\n","      etiqueta = max(lista_etiquetas,\n","                     key=lista_etiquetas.count)\n","    mapa_etiquetas[fila][col] = etiqueta\n","\n","print(mapa_etiquetas)"],"metadata":{"id":"fiaGDPuTcdcw"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# mapa de colores\n","title = ('Iteración ' + str(max_iters))\n","cmap = colors.ListedColormap(\n","    ['tab:green', 'tab:orange', 'tab:blue'])\n","plt.imshow(mapa_etiquetas, cmap=cmap)\n","plt.colorbar()\n","plt.title(title)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"9bazrrgJcfZA"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# etapa de prueba\n","\n","# normalización de datos de prueba\n","datos_pruebas = normalizacion(test_x)\n","\n","# inicialización\n","etiquetas_ganadoras = []\n","\n","# aplicación de SOM\n","for t in range(datos_pruebas.shape[0]):\n"," ganadora = BMUS(datos_pruebas, t, som)\n"," row = ganadora[0]\n"," col = ganadora[1]\n"," prediccion = mapa_etiquetas[row][col]\n"," # predicciones\n"," etiquetas_ganadoras.append(prediccion)\n","\n","# muestra la medida de exactitud de SOM\n","print(\"Exactitud: \",accuracy_score(test_y,\n","      np.array(etiquetas_ganadoras)))\n"],"metadata":{"id":"X5Im-2xVckXi"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}